<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SUSCEPTIBILITY_ELEC> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Electric susceptibility is a dimensionless proportionality constant that indicates the degree of polarization of a dielectric material in response to an applied electric field. Here P = epsilon_0 * chi_e * E. Where epsilon_0 is the electric permittivity of free space (electric constant), P is the polarization density of the material chi_e is the electric susceptibility and E is the electric field."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
