<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroCi> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Another commonly used measure of radioactivity, the microcurie: $1 \\micro Ci = 3.7 \\times 10 disintegrations per second = 2.22 \\times 10 disintegrations per minute$. A radiotherapy machine may have roughly 1000 Ci of a radioisotope such as caesium-137 or cobalt-60. This quantity of radioactivity can produce serious health effects with only a few minutes of close-range, un-shielded exposure. The typical human body contains roughly $0.1\\micro Ci$ of naturally occurring potassium-40. " .
