<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/C-PER-MOL> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> " ($C/mol$) is a unit in the category of Molar electric charge. It is also known as $coulombs/mol$. Coulomb Per Mol has a dimension of $TN{-1}I$ where $T$ is time, $N$ is amount of substance, and $I$ is electric current. This unit is the standard SI unit in this category." .
