<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliARCSEC> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A minute of arc, arcminute, or minute arc (MOA), is a unit of angular measurement equal to one sixtieth (1/60) of one degree (circle/21,600), or $\\pi /10,800 radians$. In turn, a second of arc or arcsecond is one sixtieth (1/60) of one minute of arc. Since one degree is defined as one three hundred and sixtieth (1/360) of a rotation, one minute of arc is 1/21,600 of a rotation.  the milliarcsecond, abbreviated mas, is used in astronomy." .
