<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NCM_1ATM_0DEG_C_NL> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "\nThe $\\textit{normal cubic metre}$ is a unit for liquid products conforming to the Dutch Mining Regulations (Mijnbouwregeling) for reporting in the Dutch oil and gas industry, and used predominantly for crude oil. As such, it is a measure of the actual amount of oil, not the volume of the oil. The reference conditions for a Dutch normal cubic metre are 0 degrees Celsius at 1 standard atmosphere (atm), equivalent to 101.325 kilopascals (kPa) of pressure.\n  " .
